From: Wren <wren@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] JSC: initialise the metadata-table value profiles to the empty JSValue on JSVALUE32_64

2.54 keeps the value profiles in the zero-filled front part of the MetadataTable (UnlinkedMetadataTable::link()
memsets them to 0). A zeroed bucket is the empty JSValue only where JSValue::encode(JSValue()) == 0 (64-bit). On
JSVALUE32_64 the empty value has EmptyValueTag != 0, so a zeroed bucket decodes as the double +0.0: every
never-sampled profile predicted AnyIntAsDouble instead of "no information", and the DFG compiled never-executed
code as if it had seen doubles. Observable failure: Map.prototype.forEach (builtin, @mapIterationEntry(storage) + 1
passed back to the host function @mapIterationNext) was compiled with a double-typed `entry`, the host function read
its low word (0) and iterated entry 0 forever once the DFG had compiled forEach with low tier-up thresholds.

Construct the buckets with the ValueProfile constructor (clearBuckets) after the memset on 32-bit.
---
diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/UnlinkedMetadataTableInlines.h b/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/UnlinkedMetadataTableInlines.h
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/UnlinkedMetadataTableInlines.h
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/bytecode/UnlinkedMetadataTableInlines.h
@@ -137,6 +137,14 @@
     }
     // FIXME: Is this needed since we'll clear the data in the CodeBlock Constructor... Plus I could see caching value profiles being profitable.
     memset(buffer, 0, valueProfileSize);
+#if USE(JSVALUE32_64)
+    // A zeroed bucket is the empty JSValue only where JSValue::encode(JSValue()) == 0 (64-bit). On JSVALUE32_64
+    // EmptyValueTag != 0, so a zeroed bucket reads as the double +0.0: every never-sampled profile would predict
+    // AnyIntAsDouble instead of "no information", and the DFG then feeds doubles to host functions that need an
+    // int32 (e.g. @mapIterationNext(storage, entry) in Map.prototype.forEach looped forever on entry == 0).
+    for (unsigned offset = 0; offset < valueProfileSize; offset += sizeof(ValueProfile))
+        new (NotNull, buffer + offset) ValueProfile();
+#endif
     memset(buffer + valueProfileSize + sizeof(LinkingData) + offsetTableSize, 0, totalSize - offsetTableSize - valueProfileSize);
     return adoptRef(*new (buffer + valueProfileSize + sizeof(LinkingData)) MetadataTable(*this));
 }
